  "scope": "Exact 3fe2b0ca tapered candidate versus 59efceaf 12% reference, with selected bind/skeleton, 45/90-degree, focused and oblique joint views. No game motion, dressed appearance or final contact qualification.",
  "observations": [
    "The inspected rest silhouette, skeleton placement and foot positions are preserved. Selected 45-degree poses do not show a new gross collapse.",
    "The taper reduces the measured intersection counts, but the paired close and oblique views do not establish a convincing visual correction of the compressed shoulder and hip/groin transitions. The base/rig deformation gate remains failed; do not advance to final game clips or appearance fitting.",
    "Both diagnostic clip exports reproduce every saved 45/90-degree intersection count. The whole-body/detail run has 60 views and the matching oblique supplement has eight, both with zero browser errors.",
    "The prior static repair windows were derived from posed contact bounds while weight selection occurred on the rest mesh. The new contact map records distinct rest/posed bounds and 517 source-bound vertex records; further repair must consume exact rest-space correspondence instead of treating posed bounds as a rest mask.",
    "Residual shoulder contacts are now led by bone_2/upper-arm pairs (68 left and 39 right). The old Spine donor role maps to bone_1, so bone_2 was not included in that recipe. Hip contacts remain led by Hips/thigh pairs (157 left and 71 right), with additional thigh self-folds."
  ],
  "decision": "Another isolated joint repair is required before full animation processing; do not qualify or publish the tapered candidate.",
  "next_repair_plan": [
    "Use exact tapered GLB 3fe2b0ca and verify contact-map source hash, per-mesh vertex index, rest position and weight signature before editing any mapped vertex.",
    "Isolate an additional intermediate torso bone_2-to-upper-arm transfer on the verified shoulder contact patches with smooth mesh-neighbor falloff; record its fraction and mask explicitly. Keep hip changes in a separate experiment.",
    "Reproduce both frozen comparisons, preserve rest geometry, export/reimport, and repeat all 16 arm/leg bends, normalized/influence checks and visual comparison. Reject regressions and retain prior candidates.",
    "Then investigate remaining hip Hips/thigh weighting or topology on its own mapped contact patches. Connect the full cloud repair/retarget/animation path only after controlled shape quality passes."
  ],
